"Majority out-dominating sets in digraphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.0479)\nciteturn2academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.0 years ago; Title: Majority out-dominating sets in digraphs ... $ The minimum cardinality of a MODS in $D$ is the {\\it set majority out-domination number} $\\gamma^+_{m}(D)$ of $D.\nTitle: Majority out-dominating sets in digraphs\nAuthors: Karam Ebadi, Martín Manrique, Reza Jafary, J. Joseline Manora\nDate: Sun Nov  3 15:36:09 2013\n\nThe concept of majority domination in graphs has been defined in at least two different ways: As a function and as a set. In this work we extend the latter concept to digraphs, while the former was extended in another paper. Given a digraph $D=(V,A),$ a set $S\\subseteq V$ is a \\textit{majority out-dominating set} (MODS) of $D$ if $|N^+[S]|\\geq \\frac {n}{2}.$ The minimum cardinality of a MODS in $D$ is the {\\it set majority out-domination number} $\\gamma^+_{m}(D)$ of $D.$ In this work we introduce these concepts and prove some results about them, among which the characterization of minimal MODSs.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStructures of Domination in Graphs | Springer Nature Link (https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-58892-2)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.5 years ago; Crawled: last week; The second part covers domination in hypergraphs, chessboards, and digraphs and tournaments. ... Haynes is also a co-author  of  the Springer Briefs in Mathematics  From Domination to Coloring: The Graph Theory of Stephen T. ... Henning has devoted much of his research interests to the field of domination theory in graphs. ... Hedetniemi and co-authored  the Springer Monographs in Mathematics book Total Domination in Graphs  and in 2020, he co-authored Springer’s Developments in Mathematics book Transversals in Linear Uniform Hypergraphs.\n\n# Structures of Domination in Graphs\n\n  * Book\n  * © 2021\n\nStructures of Domination in Graphs\n\n## Overview\n\nEditors:\n    \n\n  * Teresa W. Haynes ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0865-0871^{0},\n  * Stephen T. Hedetniemi^{1},\n  * Michael A. Henning ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8185-067X^{2}\n\n  * Surveys include known results with sample proof techniques for each parameter\n  * Provides a reference for established researchers and graduate students\n  * First chapter includes a glossary of commonly used terms\n\nPart of the book series: Developments in Mathematics (DEVM, volume 66)\n\n## About this book\n\nThis volume comprises 17 contributions that present advanced topics in graph domination, featuring open problems, modern techniques, and recent results.   The book is divided into 3 parts. The first part focuses on several domination-related concepts: broadcast domination, alliances, domatic numbers, dominator colorings, irredundance in graphs, private neighbor concepts, game domination, varieties of Roman domination and spectral graph theory. The second part covers domination in hypergraphs, chessboards, and digraphs and tournaments. The third part focuses on the development of algorithms and complexity of  signed, minus and majority domination, power domination, and alliances in graphs. The third part also includes a chapter on self-stabilizing algorithms. Of extra benefit to the reader, the first chapter includes a glossary of commonly used terms.\n\nThe book is intended to provide a reference for established researchers in the fields of domination and graph theory and graduate students who wish to gain knowledge of the topics covered as well as an overview of the major accomplishments and proof techniques used in the field. \n\n## Table of contents (17 chapters)\n\n  1. ### Front Matter\n\nPages i-viii\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n  2. ### Glossary of Common Terms\n\n     * Teresa W. Haynes, Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Michael A. Henning\n\nPages 1-11\n\n  3. ### Related Parameters\n\n    1. #### Front Matter\n\nPages 13-13\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n    2. #### Broadcast Domination in Graphs\n\n       * Michael A. Henning, Gary MacGillivray, Feiran Yang\n\nPages 15-46\n\n    3. #### Alliances and Related Domination Parameters\n\n       * Teresa W. Haynes, Stephen T. Hedetniemi\n\nPages 47-77\n\n    4. #### Fractional Domatic, Idomatic, and Total Domatic Numbers of a Graph\n\n       * Wayne Goddard, Michael A. Henning\n\nPages 79-99\n\n    5. #### Dominator and Total Dominator Colorings in Graphs\n\n       * Michael A. Henning\n\nPages 101-133\n\n    6. #### Irredundance\n\n       * C. M. Mynhardt, A. Roux\n\nPages 135-181\n\n    7. #### The Private Neighbor Concept\n\n       * Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Alice A. McRae, Raghuveer Mohan\n\nPages 183-218\n\n    8. #### An Introduction to Game Domination in Graphs\n\n       * Michael A. Henning\n\nPages 219-243\n\n    9. #### Domination and Spectral Graph Theory\n\n       * Carlos Hoppen, David P. Jacobs, Vilmar Trevisan\n\nPages 245-272\n\n    10. #### Varieties of Roman Domination\n\n       * M. Chellali, N. Jafari Rad, S. M. Sheikholeslami, L. Volkmann\n\nPages 273-307\n\n  4. ### Domination in Selected Graph Families\n\n    1. #### Front Matter\n\nPages 309-309\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n    2. #### Domination and Total Domination in Hypergraphs\n\n       * Michael A. Henning, Anders Yeo\n\nPages 311-339\n\n    3. #### Domination in Chessboards\n\n       * Jason T. Hedetniemi, Stephen T. Hedetniemi\n\nPages 341-386\n\n    4. #### Domination in Digraphs\n\n       * Teresa W. Haynes, Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Michael A. Henning\n\nPages 387-428\n\n  5. ### Algorithms and Complexity\n\n    1. #### Front Matter\n\nPages 309-309\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n    2. #### Algorithms and Complexity of Signed, Minus, and Majority Domination\n\n       * Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Alice A. McRae, Raghuveer Mohan\n\nPages 431-460\n\n    3. #### Algorithms and Complexity of Power Domination in Graphs\n\n       * Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Alice A. McRae, Raghuveer Mohan\n\nPages 461-484\n\n    4. #### Self-Stabilizing Domination Algorithms\n\n       * Stephen T. Hedetniemi\n\nPages 485-520\nHe co-authored a Springer Briefs in Mathematics   From Domination to Coloring: The Graph Theory of Stephen T. Hedetniemi and co-authored  the Springer Monographs in Mathematics book Total Domination in Graphs  and in 2020, he co-authored Springer’s Developments in Mathematics book Transversals in Linear Uniform Hypergraphs.\n\n## Bibliographic information\n\n  * Book title: Structures of Domination in Graphs\n\n  * Editors: Teresa W. Haynes, Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Michael A. Henning\n\n  * Series title: Developments in Mathematics\n\n  * DOI: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-58892-2\n\n  * Publisher: Springer Cham\n\n  * eBook packages: Mathematics and Statistics, Mathematics and Statistics (R0)\n\n  * Copyright information: The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2021\n\n  * Hardcover ISBN: 978-3-030-58891-5 Published: 05 May 2021\n\n  * Softcover ISBN: 978-3-030-58894-6 Published: 05 May 2022\n\n  * eBook ISBN: 978-3-030-58892-2 Published: 04 May 2021\n\n  * Series ISSN: 1389-2177\n\n  * Series E-ISSN: 2197-795X\n\n  * Edition number: 1\n\n  * Number of pages: VIII, 536\n\n  * Number of illustrations: 108 b/w illustrations, 61 illustrations in colour\n\n  * Topics: Graph Theory\n\n## Keywords\n\n  * Domination Frameworks\n  * Irredundance\n  * Alliances in Graphs\n  * Stratified Domination\n  * Strong and weak domination\n  * Graph Partitions\n  * Grundy colorings\n  * Hypergraphs\n  * Domination in Chessboards\n  * Digraphs\n  * Self-Stabilizing Algorithms\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDiscrete Applied Mathematics 284 (2020) 42–52 (https://perso.limos.fr/ffoucaud/Publications/Papers/J32_LD-digraphs_DAM_2020.pdf)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Received in revised form 20 February 2020 ... in graph theory: see the two classic books [10,11] on the subject. ... in undirected graphs, domination in digraphs is less studied; we refer to the papers [8,14,15] for some examples.\nDiscrete Applied Mathematics 284 (2020) 42–52\nContents lists available at ScienceDirect\nDiscrete Applied Mathematics\njournal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/dam\nDomination and location in twin-free digraphs\nFlorent Foucaud a,b,1, Shahrzad Heydarshahi b,∗, Aline Parreau c\na Univ. Bordeaux, Bordeaux INP, CNRS, LaBRI, UMR5800, F-33400 Talence, France\nb Univ. Orléans, INSA Centre Val de Loire, LIFO EA 4022, F-45067 Orléans Cedex 2, France\nc Univ Lyon, Université Claude Bernard, CNRS, LIRIS - UMR 5205, F69622, France\na r t i c l e\ni n f o\na b s t r a c t\nArticle history:\nReceived 14 December 2018\nReceived in revised form 20 February 2020\nAccepted 4 March 2020\nAvailable online 12 March 2020\nKeywords:\nDigraphs\nDominating sets\nLocating-dominating sets\nBounds\nA dominating set D in a digraph is a set of vertices such that every vertex is either in D or\nhas an in-neighbour in D. A dominating set D of a digraph is locating-dominating if every\nvertex not in D has a unique set of in-neighbours within D. The location-domination\nThe\ndomination number γ (G) of G is the smallest size of a dominating set of G. The area of domination is one of the main topics\nin graph theory: see the two classic books [10,11] on the subject. While there are hundreds of papers on domination\nin undirected graphs, domination in digraphs is less studied; we refer to the papers [8,14,15] for some examples. One\nparticular variation of domination is the concept of location-domination, introduced by Slater for undirected graphs in [19]\n(see also [17,18]). For a set S of vertices of a digraph G, two vertices x and y of V(G)\\ S are located by S if there is a vertex\nof S that is an in-neighbour of exactly one vertex among x and y. The set S is a locating set of G if it locates all the\npairs of V(G) \\ S (but does not necessarily dominate the graph). Equivalently, every vertex not in S has a distinct set of\nin-neighbours in S. The location number of a graph G is the size of a smallest locating set and is denoted by loc(G). A set\nD of vertices of a digraph G is locating-dominating if it is both locating and dominating. The location-domination number\nγL(G) of a digraph G is the smallest size of a locating-dominating set of G. Note that γL(G) −1 ≤loc(G) ≤γL(G), since at\nmost one vertex is not dominated in a locating set.\n∗Corresponding author.\nE-mail addresses:\nflorent.foucaud@gmail.fr (F. Foucaud), shahrzad.heydarshahi@univ-orleans.fr (S. Heydarshahi), aline.parreau@univ-lyon1.fr\n(A. Parreau).\n1 This author is partially supported by the ANR project HOSIGRA (ANR-17-CE40-0022) and the IFCAM, India project ‘‘Applications of graph\nhomomorphisms’’ (MA/IFCAM/18/39).\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2020.03.025\n0166-218X/© 2020 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDomination in Digraphs (https://ouci.dntb.gov.ua/en/works/4ryWXVL7/)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Domination in Digraphs ... 2020, Developments in Mathematics Structures of Domination in Graphs, p. ... Haynes, Stephen T. ... Henning\n\n# Domination in Digraphs\n\n## General information\n\nPublication type\n\nBook Chapter\n\nDOI\n\n10.1007/978-3-030-58892-2_13\n\nJournal\n\n2020, Developments in Mathematics Structures of Domination in Graphs, p. 387-428\n\nPublisher\n\nSpringer International Publishing\n\nAuthors\n\nTeresa W. Haynes, Stephen T. Hedetniemi, Michael A. Henning\n\n## Details\n\nNumber of citations\n\n2\n\nNumber of works in the list of references\n\n93\n\nIndexed in Scopus\n\nYes\n\nIndexed in Web of Science\n\nNo\n\n## List of references\n\n  1. N. Alon, J. Balogh, B. Bollobás, T. Szabó, Game domination number. Discrete Math. 256, 23–33 (2002)\nDOI: 10.1016/S0012-365X(00)00358-7\n  2. N. Alo